// This is a static asset migration task
// The source file is a PNG image that needs to be copied to the Angular assets directory
// No code conversion is needed for binary files like images

// In Angular CLI projects, static assets like images are stored in the src/assets directory
// The migration plan indicates that project-logo.png should be moved from the root directory
// to src/assets/images/project-logo.png

// Steps to complete this migration:
// 1. Create the directory structure if it doesn't exist:
//    mkdir -p src/assets/images
// 
// 2. Copy the file to the new location:
//    cp project-logo.png src/assets/images/
//
// 3. Update any references to this image in your application:
//    - In AngularJS, the image might have been referenced as: 
//      <img src="project-logo.png">
//    - In Angular, it should be referenced as:
//      <img src="assets/images/project-logo.png">
//
// 4. If using the Angular CLI, make sure the assets array in angular.json includes this path:
//    "assets": [
//      "src/favicon.ico",
//      "src/assets"
//    ]
//
// No TypeScript code conversion is needed for this binary file.